  "description": "Golden vectors for the three rules two layers must compute the same way (docs/STORE.md section 6). The Python side is plugins/boopis/tests/test_store_plan.py, the Rust side is workstream A's. `tree_hash`: sha256 over the lines `<relative path, POSIX>\\0<sha256 of the file's bytes>` joined by `\\n`, for every regular file under the root, in the order of Python's PurePath comparison (path components compared one by one, so `a/b.txt` sorts before `a-b.txt`), leaving out any path with a `.git` component, a file that cannot be read counting as the word `unreadable`; empty folders, modes and times do not count; a link to a file inside the tree is read as that file. `canonical`: keys sorted, `,` and `:` without spaces, UTF-8 characters kept as they are (not \\u-escaped), control characters escaped as JSON does. `plugin_hash`: sha256 of the canonical JSON of a PluginPlan without `plugin_hash`.",
